# Normalize line endings.
#
# This working tree is shared between Windows and Linux (it lives on an NTFS
# partition mounted by both). Without this, Windows git checks files out with
# CRLF while Linux git expects LF, so every tracked file shows as modified after
# switching OS - 14 files with 3912 identical insertions and deletions, and no
# real content change.
#
# text=auto lets git detect text vs binary (binaries are left untouched);
# eol=lf stores AND checks out text files with LF on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf
